\f3\fs26 When Cracker woke he felt good. Fantastic in fact. He didn\'92t cough up anything black or brown just a healthy yellowy-green. He had not hacked up anything green since he was a kid. His back was straight and erect, no pain whatsoever and neck movement was unhindered and fluid. Carved from ivory, his morning erection was busting against the inside of his shorts, desperately waiting to announce itself to the world. Ordinarily, he spent the first 20 minutes of the day coughing, gagging and dry retching, but today he felt hungry and actually looked forward to breaking his fast. Then he caught a glimpse of himself in the mirror and saw his face was, for want of a better term, normal. In truth better than normal, he had actual colour in his cheeks, his eyes were sparkling and teeth gleaming. All of the injuries from the explosion were, inexplicably, faded and almost gone. \
\'93What the fuck, Sarah?\'94 Cracker smiled. His hair was still a bit patchy, but in staring he could swear it was growing before his very eyes. \'93Sarah!\'94 He called out, unable to drag himself away from the mirror. It had been many years since he looked this good. She appeared almost immediately at the yellow stained bathroom door and upon seeing Cracker screamed loud and long.\
\'93Oh, no. This is not good. Not good at all.\'94 She, too, was looking great and seemed to have shaken whatever had ailed her the night previous. The nausea and stomach cramps all a vague memory.\
\'93What\'92s the problem? I feel fantastic.\'94 Cracker flexed his biceps. \'93Check out them cannons.\'94\
 \'93The disc has done something to you.\'94 Trying to impress a sense of urgency, but prudently neglecting to tell Cracker the contagion she carried had, no doubt, invaded his system and caused the overnight makeover. The infection was progressing rapidly, just as she would have expected. Inside her body the virus operated in an entirely positive way, but the long term effects on Cracker\'92s constitution was anyone\'92s guess. She had feared for decades, when she finally erred and unleashed danger upon others, the moment when she had to either come clean or manufacture some credible fiction. Shrewdly, she had ignored instinct and decided to fictionalise, blaming the disc. 
\f4\i The truth can wait for another day. Not too soon I hope.
\f3\i0 \
\'93If this is sick, then bring it on.\'94 Cracker did not see a problem.\
\'93We cannot assume that your current symptoms will last. We should assume that you might pass it on to others. No exchanging body fluids with anyone.\'94 She did not like misleading him, or anyone else for that matter, but she had to ensure Cracker would not infect others. \
\'93No sex then?\'94\
\'93No sex or anything else.\'94 She rubbed her right breast, the pain was gone, but the disgust remained. Cracker\'92s hand automatically raised for a high-five but he was, yet again, denied.\
\'93No sex? That should not be too much of a problem.\'94 Cracker wasn\'92t exactly a lady\'92s man and had come to terms with his lack of appeal. \'93I don\'92t suppose there is any reason to think my system is free of the goop?\'94\
\'93The drastic changes in your appearance cannot be ignored.\'94 She left it at that. \
